{
  Ciphertext x("x");
  Plaintext alpha("alpha");
  Plaintext c0("c0");
  Plaintext c1("c1");
  Plaintext c3("c3");
  Plaintext c5("c5");
  Ciphertext z = x * alpha;
  Ciphertext u = z * z;
  Ciphertext w = z * u;
  Ciphertext uw = u * w;
  Ciphertext a2 = uw + uw;
  Ciphertext a4 = a2 + a2;
  Ciphertext a8 = a4 + a4;
  Ciphertext a16 = a8 + a8;
  Ciphertext w2 = w + w;
  Ciphertext w4 = w2 + w2;
  Ciphertext w8 = w4 + w4;
  Ciphertext w16 = w8 + w8;
  Ciphertext w20 = w16 + w4;
  Ciphertext z2 = z + z;
  Ciphertext z4 = z2 + z2;
  Ciphertext z3x = z4 - z;
  Ciphertext z5 = z4 + z;
  Ciphertext e3 = w4 - z3x;
  Ciphertext e5 = a16 + z5 - w20;
  Ciphertext r = z * c1 + e3 * c3 + e5 * c5 + c0;
  r.set_output("y");
}
```

The z⁵ part is now built from s = c5·w (w = z³) as 16·s·u − 20·s, which reuses s and drops the separate uw product and the w20 chain. The c3 part and the 5·c5·z term stay as cheap plaintext multiplies at different levels.

